Here's how to implement this in .NET MAUI Shell:

## 1. Override `OnBackButtonPressed` in your page

```csharp
// EditProductPage.xaml.cs
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            // Fire-and-forget since the override is synchronous
            ConfirmDiscardAsync();
            return true; // Cancel default navigation
        }
        return base.OnBackButtonPressed();
    }

    private async Task ConfirmDiscardAsync()
    {
        bool discard = await DisplayAlert(
            "Unsaved Changes",
            "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
            "Discard", "Stay");

        if (discard)
            await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    }
}
```

> **Note:** `OnBackButtonPressed` only fires for the **hardware/OS back button** (Android). It does **not** fire when the Shell navigation bar back arrow is tapped.

## 2. Replace the Shell back button with a custom "Cancel" toolbar item

To intercept the shell nav-bar back arrow, hide it and add your own:

```xml
<!-- EditProductPage.xaml -->
<ContentPage
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
    x:Class="MyApp.EditProductPage"
    Shell.BackButtonBehavior="{StaticResource CancelBackButton}">

    <ContentPage.Resources>
        <BackButtonBehavior x:Key="CancelBackButton"
            TextOverride="Cancel"
            Command="{Binding CancelCommand}" />
    </ContentPage.Resources>

    <!-- Or inline: -->
    <Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
        <BackButtonBehavior
            TextOverride="Cancel"
            IconOverride=""
            Command="{Binding CancelCommand}" />
    </Shell.BackButtonBehavior>

    <!-- page content -->
</ContentPage>
```

## 3. Handle the command in your ViewModel (or code-behind)

```csharp
// ViewModel approach
public ICommand CancelCommand { get; }

public EditProductViewModel()
{
    CancelCommand = new Command(async () =>
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool discard = await Shell.Current.DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!discard) return;
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    });
}
```

## Key points

| Scenario | Mechanism |
|----------|-----------|
| Android hardware back | `OnBackButtonPressed()` override |
| Shell nav-bar back arrow | `Shell.BackButtonBehavior` with custom `Command` |
| Swipe-back (iOS) | Not interceptable by Shell — disable with `Shell.PresentationMode` or platform config |

To block iOS swipe-back gestures, add in your page constructor:

```csharp
Shell.SetPresentationMode(this, PresentationMode.ModalAnimated);
```

Or on iOS specifically via a handler:

```csharp
#if IOS
Microsoft.Maui.Handlers.PageHandler.Mapper.AppendToMapping("DisableSwipeBack", (handler, view) =>
{
    handler.ViewController?.NavigationController
        ?.InteractivePopGestureRecognizer?.SetEnabled(false);
});
#endif
```

This combination covers all navigation vectors while showing "Cancel" instead of the default back arrow.
